## 4. Obligations of the builder

The builder agrees to:

1. Use the data only for the purpose described in §2, including
   model training, validation, and evaluation against the
   regulatory pathway named in §2.
2. Not attempt to re-identify any individual whose data appears in
   the dataset.
3. Apply industry-standard secure-development practices to any
   model artefact derived from the dataset, including (where
   applicable) ISO/IEC 27001 controls, AWS / GCP / Azure shared-
   responsibility-model adherence, and documented incident response.
4. **Provide a Statement of Model Provenance** to the host upon
   first commercial deployment, identifying the dataset's role in
   training/validation.
5. **Post-market monitoring**: where the deployed model is used in
   a clinical or safety context, the builder will share aggregated
   performance signals with the host on a six-month cadence, scoped
   to the data slices covered by the dataset.
6. Destroy any raw copy of the dataset within
   {{dataset.retentionDays}} days of regulatory submission OR
   model deprecation, whichever is earlier. Derived model weights
   are not subject to this destruction obligation; the raw data is.
7. Report any actual or suspected security incident affecting the
   dataset to the host within 72 hours of discovery.

## 5. Royalty and revenue terms

{{#if dataset.commercialUseTerms.requiresRoyalty}}
The dataset's terms include a royalty obligation. The specific
percentage and accounting cadence are negotiated separately and
attached as **Annex A** to this agreement before signature.
{{else}}
The dataset's terms do **not** include a royalty obligation. The
builder retains commercial rights to model artefacts derived from
the dataset, subject to the obligations in §4.
{{/if}}

## 6. Audit and inspection

The host reserves the right to request, on no more than an annual
basis and with 30 days' notice, evidence that the builder is
operating within the obligations in §4 and §5. The builder will
provide such evidence in a form proportionate to the request.

## 7. Liability and warranty

The dataset is provided "as is". The host disclaims warranty as to
the fitness of the dataset for any clinical, diagnostic, or
treatment decision. The builder bears sole responsibility for
clinical validation and regulatory compliance of any model
deployed in a clinical setting.

## 8. Term and termination

This agreement is effective from the date above and continues for
the duration of the access grant or until terminated by either
party in writing. The obligations under §4(2), §4(4), §4(5), and
§5 survive termination indefinitely.

## 9. Governing law

This agreement is governed by the law of the host institution's
primary place of establishment. Disputes are subject to the
exclusive jurisdiction of that court.

